{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/807331-gift-of-the-elementals-how-to-use-it","id":807331,"title":"Gift of the Elementals: How to use it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-12T15:05:32-08:00","id":807331,"title":"Gift of the Elementals: How to use it?","content":"I've been searching in the forums about Influences, but couldn't find anything.<br /> <br /> First question, what book best describes the effects of Influences? I have Book of Spirits and did not find extensive information on the subject, touching just as much as Werewolf: The Forsaken 2e. I do think I got the general idea of what Influences do, but I want to know what you guys allow players to accomplish by using the Facets of the Gift of the Elementals.<br /> <br /> First Dot should be easy, as it just strengthens the concept affected. Fire would get bigger and deal more damage, water would overflow and maybe get purified, earth would get denser and more resistant, and air would allow for increasing wind currents to push someone and fresher air, but how do we progress from here? Can Manipulate Fire make it jump from a torch to the face of the intruder across the room? Can Earth Facet be used upon rocks and stone to sculpt them instantly? Do I need Create do get a little bit of water in the middle of the desert or I could extract it from the air's humidity and form a small puddle using Manipulate? At which level may I use air to make a whirlwind? Can I control it somehow? I can't find some examples on how much each level can do, making it hard to rule what to roll to accomplish anything.<br /> <br /> Also, how do you guys allow them to interact with Catastrophe? The first three levels of Tongue of Fire would be useless as there is hardly any fire to affect, even in such a large radius. You could argue that someone cooking might get burned, but the Uratha has no reliable way to tell if there is fire somewhere. Water and air are a lot more useful, with heavy winds achievable since level 1, as lesser floods if rivers and lakes are nearby. Earth seems pointless until you can control it, making it softer to engulf people or a huge earth quake.<br /> Those effects seem to be instant, so it would be more of an earth explosion than an prolonged earthquake. Rivers would instantly swallow cities. Would you allow a tornado to be brought through this? Could the Werewolf turn a whole city block into a huge crater with Flesh of Earth?<br /> <br /> On top of that, I'm curious: Which scenes have you told about the use of those powers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T15:22:11-08:00","id":807345,"title":"","content":"You might check <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/428559-gift-of-the-elementals-question\">this thread</a>, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts\">this other one</a> for advice regarding Gift of the Elements and the Influences involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T15:41:18-08:00","id":807358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/807331-gift-of-the-elementals-how-to-use-it?p=807345#post807345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might check <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/428559-gift-of-the-elementals-question\">this thread</a>, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/471285-on-the-innovative-use-of-elemental-gifts\">this other one</a> for advice regarding Gift of the Elements and the Influences involved.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you, I'm checking them out right now!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T04:08:31-08:00","id":807766,"title":"","content":"I'm now picturing really old werewolves complaining about how Tongue of Flame + Catastrophe was a lot more effective 100 years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T06:54:46-08:00","id":807840,"title":"","content":"&quot;And that, young pup, is how my father started the Great Fire of London. Don't look at me like that, it's the only <i>gathra </i>a local <i>Dihir </i>would accept.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T14:33:33-08:00","id":808238,"title":"","content":"Would other Gifts along those lines be acceptable?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Gift of Emotion</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Cunning Facet: Touch of Joy</b><br /> Influence Happiness, easily used to beguile the prey into thinking it is safer than it really is. With mastery if can also become a power of sorrow, when happiness is controlled into sadness.<br /> <br /> <b>Glory: Den of Sentiment</b><br /> Focused on an area imbued with the desired emotion. People that enter the area are affected by environmental tilts. May also be used to infuse an object with the desired emotion, infecting people who come in contact with the object.<br /> <br /> <b>Honor Facet: Whisper of Wrath</b><br /> Influence Wrath, giving Uratha some sort of ability to &quot;ride the wave&quot; of Kuruth, like vampires? With mastery it becomes a power of tranquility, when wrath is controlled into calm.<br /> <br /> <b>Purity Facet: Glimpse of Terror</b><br /> Influence Fear, boosting the already powerful weapons of the People against lesser prey, and extending the use of fear to intimidate even the greatest predators. With mastery becomes the power of courage, when fear is controlled into bravery.<br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom: Taste of Disgust</b><br /> Influence Disgust, mainly used to keep unwanted attention away from you or anything you want to protect. Also very useful to break relationships, as aversion can rapidly grow into distrust. With mastery it becomes the power of appeal, from where some of the legends about love potions come from. </div> </div> </div>I don't know if those are powerful enough to compare with Elementals, but you get the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T15:45:54-08:00","id":808288,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, I saw the Gift of emotion and had to laugh hysterically. Because all I can think of is Inside Out, and how this gift forces one of the emotions to take the wheel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8122-archonares","name":"ArchonAres","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T15:49:31-08:00","id":808294,"title":"","content":"Werewolves kinda already have emotion manipulation with their lunacy-modifying facets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T16:44:21-08:00","id":808310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/807331-gift-of-the-elementals-how-to-use-it?p=808288#post808288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, I saw the Gift of emotion and had to laugh hysterically. Because all I can think of is Inside Out, and how this gift forces one of the emotions to take the wheel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't stop thinking about that, too!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/807331-gift-of-the-elementals-how-to-use-it?p=808288#post808288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Werewolves kinda already have emotion manipulation with their lunacy-modifying facets.</span><br /> </span><br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna read through them again. However, I just set those up as an example that any influence could become a Gift that way. It feels strange though, kinda like giving a Mage vibe to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T17:48:54-08:00","id":808343,"title":"","content":"There's also the Rage Gifts. You could probably have flat out Sadness, Joy and Fear Gifts as well, if you're particularly creative. Disgust, too. If you want to go further you could have Greed, Hope, Love and Compassion Gifts. Or Unity, Trust and Reward. Or Cowardice, Hatred and Falsehood. Or Control, Patience and Diligence.<br /> <br /> The seeming infinite possibilities really drew me to Werewolf from the get-go. Spirits as they are reflect basically everything that exists in one form or another, even as a concept. And potentially there's a gift for everything, providing you can manage to find a way to focus the hunt through it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-13-2016, 08:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T23:44:59-08:00","id":808490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/807331-gift-of-the-elementals-how-to-use-it?p=808310#post808310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't stop thinking about that, too!</div> </div> </div> </div>Using Sadness as the multiplier makes a delightful amount of sense, given the movie. I'd probably rearrange which Renown mapped to which Emotion, because you've got some very specific use cases whereas the utility of an Influence is much broader, but that's just me nitpicking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T03:21:47-08:00","id":808551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArchonAres</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/807331-gift-of-the-elementals-how-to-use-it?p=808288#post808288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, I saw the Gift of emotion and had to laugh hysterically. Because all I can think of is Inside Out, and how this gift forces one of the emotions to take the wheel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cats are immune to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T07:56:19-08:00","id":808696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/807331-gift-of-the-elementals-how-to-use-it?p=808343#post808343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also the Rage Gifts. You could probably have flat out Sadness, Joy and Fear Gifts as well, if you're particularly creative. Disgust, too. If you want to go further you could have Greed, Hope, Love and Compassion Gifts. Or Unity, Trust and Reward. Or Cowardice, Hatred and Falsehood. Or Control, Patience and Diligence.<br /> <br /> The seeming infinite possibilities really drew me to Werewolf from the get-go. Spirits as they are reflect basically everything that exists in one form or another, even as a concept. And potentially there's a gift for everything, providing you can manage to find a way to focus the hunt through it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your point about each emotion being a complete Gift seems valid, but the other way around seems, too. Cound't Elementals be split into four Gifts? Gift of Flame, Gift of Water, etc. Maybe even going to Gift of Ice or Cold. It has been hard for me to decide whether the scope of a Gift should be broad or narrow. If you take the Elementals as an example, the scope of each Facet is increadibly broad, allowing for an elasticity of power that even Mages might envy. However, the majority of the other Gifts have narrower Facets, controlling very specific situations like &quot;Removing Uratha from <i>Wasu-Im</i>&quot; or &quot;Adding Glory as Strength&quot;. I like to design broader powers be default, but I can't decide if that goes well with Werewolf. Shound't this be the scope of Rites?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/807331-gift-of-the-elementals-how-to-use-it?p=808343#post808343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd probably rearrange which Renown mapped to which Emotion, because you've got some very specific use cases whereas the utility of an Influence is much broader, but that's just me nitpicking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I wasn't very clear. The description was meant to give an idea of what the Facet is capable, not to limit it. How would you rearrange the emotions? I could easily see Wisdom being Fear and Purity being Disgust, but Cunning being linked to Joy really ressonates to me. A predator using pleasure to make the prey lower it's defences is feels very cunning. Glory could handle Wrath, and &quot;Den of Sentiment&quot; could be swapped by another power. Creating a Spirit of based on the emotions was one of my first ideas, but it seemed a little powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T08:54:13-08:00","id":808743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/807331-gift-of-the-elementals-how-to-use-it?p=808696#post808696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your point about each emotion being a complete Gift seems valid, but the other way around seems, too. Cound't Elementals be split into four Gifts? Gift of Flame, Gift of Water, etc. Maybe even going to Gift of Ice or Cold. It has been hard for me to decide whether the scope of a Gift should be broad or narrow. If you take the Elementals as an example, the scope of each Facet is increadibly broad, allowing for an elasticity of power that even Mages might envy. However, the majority of the other Gifts have narrower Facets, controlling very specific situations like &quot;Removing Uratha from <i>Wasu-Im</i>&quot; or &quot;Adding Glory as Strength&quot;. I like to design broader powers be default, but I can't decide if that goes well with Werewolf. Shound't this be the scope of Rites?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just it, they can be broad or narrow. Elements is wildly broad, but you can easily have a Fire Gift, a Water Gift, and even further Ice and Mist and Ocean Gifts.<br /> <br /> The hard part is thinking of the powers for the gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-14-2016, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T05:11:39-08:00","id":809512,"title":"","content":"alternatively, each element can be assigned an emotion with a fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T05:22:01-08:00","id":810182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/807331-gift-of-the-elementals-how-to-use-it?p=809512#post809512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">alternatively, each element can be assigned an emotion with a fetish.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've read about it in another topic, but couldn't find it in the book. Can you point me the specific pages, please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby